.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH voltkit-color 1  "Voltkit 0.2.1" "Voltkit Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
voltkit\-color \- Convert a color (#hex or rgb(...)) and report WCAG contrast
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit color\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert a color (#hex or rgb(...)) and report WCAG contrast
.PP
Prints the color as HEX, RGB and HSL, and its WCAG 2.x contrast ratio as text on white and on black.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
#rgb, #rrggbb (the # is optional) or rgb(r, g, b)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "CONTRAST LEVELS"
.PP
Ratings are for normal\-size text under WCAG 2.x:
.TP
\fBAAA\fR
7:1 or higher.
.TP
\fBAA\fR
4.5:1 or higher.
.TP
\fBAA Large\fR
3:1 or higher; passes only for large text (18pt, or 14pt bold).
.TP
\fBFail\fR
Below 3:1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Hex with or without #, short or long form:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit color f80\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Functional notation:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit color \*(Aqrgb(51, 130, 202)\*(Aq\fR
.fi
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBvoltkit\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
